    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.statusline\n\n### Description\n\nHi @echasnovski,\n\nI was looking for a way to do a top line on windows in nvim, and realised that nvim has `vim.o.winbar`, which is basically what I was after. I think implementing support for it is a low hanging fruit, since it would basically just be setting it up if any of the options for it are present. I am more than willing to implement it if it aligns with the plugin  direction. Wdyt? ",
