            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nThere is a different plan for winbars within 'mini.nvim' (see #983). So I am afraid this is out of scope for 'mini.statusline'.\n\nIf you are after basically putting current statusline on top of the window, then it is already relatively easy to do by executing `vim.go.winbar = vim.go.statusline` *after* `require('mini.statusline').setup()`.",
