        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Thanks for the reply!\n\nWhat I wanted was split my info between statusline and winbar - to have git + lsp info (attached LSPs, diagnostics) in winbar and file info (name, path, type etc) + mode in the statusline. I see this is out of scope, so I'll just have to hack my own solution then - will be pretty easy thanks to the fact that statusline basically uses `nvim` native API (I've been loving how simple it is - thanks again for making the plugins!)\n\nWhen `mini.breadcrumbs` comes to life I think I would love to use it, so it would be nice if it was possible to customize the right side of `winbar` they'll take",
