        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> What I wanted was split my info between statusline and winbar - to have git + lsp info (attached LSPs, diagnostics) in winbar and file info (name, path, type etc) + mode in the statusline.\n\nYeah, this should be doable by writing own function that uses [`section_git()`](https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-statusline.html#ministatusline.section_git) and similar sections.\n\n> When `mini.breadcrumbs` comes to life I think I would love to use it, so it would be nice if it was possible to customize the right side of `winbar` they'll take\n\n*I think* it would also be out of scope by default. Probably would be possible to hack around, but definitely not by default.",
